{
  "rules": [
    "Strong positive bias: model forecasts are consistently too high versus realized prices, especially beyond ~day 10. Apply a downward level shift to the whole path, increasing with horizon.",
    "Missed regime shift / mean reversion: after the market rolls over, the model keeps projecting stable-to-rising prices. Add a mean-reversion correction that pulls forecasts toward the recent downtrend (e.g., last 10–15 day slope) rather than the prior range.",
    "Horizon-dependent error growth: early horizon (days 1–7) errors are small; mid/long horizon (days 10–30) errors become large and negative (forecast minus actual). Use a ramping correction (small at t<=7, larger by t≈30).",
    "Overshoot after local highs: when history contains a recent spike/high (e.g., ~72–73), the model extrapolates it upward, but outcomes revert sharply lower. Cap upside extrapolation and enforce reversion after highs (reduce forecast if last price is near a 30d high).",
    "Trend-lag: the model reacts too slowly to emerging declines; incorporate a momentum filter so that if recent returns are negative for several days, subtract an additional drift term from the forecast trajectory."
  ]
}
